## Not yet implemented
No live-verified chat site adapter, ChatGPT-native projects, file download/upload,
model selection, browser interruption, tool-call conversion, direct Codex OAuth,
or independent coding agent.

## Security
Do not use a real everyday Chrome profile as the Playwright persistent user
profile. CDP must stay loopback. Verify provider permissions and terms before
live automation. Never execute model instructions inside the bridge.

## Browser diagnostics policy (v0.4.2)
- A browser URL host matching chatgpt.com is not proof of a usable chat session.
- Probe UI state after bounded SPA hydration; do not mistake missing controls
  for a confirmed selector regression or completed login.
- Show only non-content DOM shape; never log page HTML, user messages,
  full URLs, cookies, local storage or account details.
- Screenshots must be explicit opt-in, local only, not overwritten, and
  reviewed by the operator before any sharing.
- No evasion of provider authentication challenges or service limits.

## v0.4.3 browser selector policy
- On an anonymous ChatGPT homepage, visible "Log in" controls mean `login_required`
  even if the public guest composer or Send control also appears.
- Prefer precise UI evidence; check multiple matches because responsive sites can
  render a hidden control before its visible equivalent.
- Logged-out fixture tests are not live authorization or capability verification.
- Never import/copy personal browser authentication material automatically.

## v0.4.4 profile and session migration
- `browser profiles`: read-only metadata discovery from bounded standard browser roots.
- `browser session import-firefox`: opt-in, allowlisted ChatGPT cookies only; source
  Firefox profile must be discovered and explicitly selected; no password access.
- Cookie values stay in-memory until installed into an OpenAgent-owned persistent
  browser context. Do not log them, export them or put them in a patch/archive.
- Cookie import is not proof of login and never overrides a provider security
  challenge. Browser-specific account restrictions and terms still apply.
- Directly launching an ordinary Firefox profile via Playwright remains unsupported.

## v0.4.5 expiry interoperability
- The allowlisted Firefox cookie importer clamps future expiry values beyond
  Playwright/Chromium year-9999 limit, and skips invalid or expired values.
- Errors from Playwright cookie insertion must not expose raw cookie data.
- Regression tests must not read real browser profiles or sessions.

## v0.4.6 homepage readiness
- Some provider UIs render Send only after the composer has content. A provider
  must explicitly opt into composer-only visual readiness. Anonymous login UI
  markers take priority; this is never proof of authentication.
- Submission requires a separate post-fill check for visible/enabled Send;
  no remote request is submitted if that check fails.

## v0.4.7 browser-turn identity
- An assistant DOM message count is not a durable conversation identity.
- When available, capture bounded `data-turn-id` / `data-message-id` values
  before submission and identify a newly mounted logical turn by unseen ID.
- Retain count-increase fallback for UIs that lack reliable stable IDs;
  a same-count replacement without IDs is ambiguous and must fail closed.
- Require turn-scoped completion evidence, stable text and no pending marker.
- No upstream conversation checkpoint/resume has been implemented by this update.
